hymus, Thymonucleic acid sodium salt\nL82: \nL83: 【11†Sign In】 to View Organizational & Contract Pricing.\nL84: ### Select a Size\nL85: \nL86: Change View\nL87: \nL88: Size/SKU  | Availability  | Price\nL89: --- | --- | ---\nL90: 50 mg D1501-50MG  | Check Cart for Availability  | $66.20\nL91: 100 mg D1501-100MG  | Check Cart for Availability  | $84.30\nL92: 500 mg D1501-500MG  | Check Cart for Availability  | $363.00\nL93: 1 g D1501-1G  | Check Cart for Availability  | $474.00\nL94: 5 g D1501-5G  | Check Cart for Availability  | $2,100.00\nL95: \nL96: * * *\nL97: ### About This Item\nL98: \nL99: CAS Number:\nL100: \nL101: 【12†73049-39-5】\nL102: \nL103: UNSPSC Code:\nL104: \nL105: 41106305\nL106: \nL107: eCl@ss:\nL108: \nL109: 32160414\nL110: \nL111: NACRES:\nL112: \nL113: NA.51\nL114: \nL115: MDL number:\nL116: \nL117: 【13†MFCD00130922】\nL118: \nL119: Form:\nL120: \nL121: fibers\nL122: \nL123: Storage temp.:\nL124: \nL125: 2-8°C\nL126: \nL127: ## D1501-50MG\nL128: \nL129: ### $66.20\nL130: \nL131: * * *\nL132: \nL133: Check Cart for Availability\nL134: \nL135: * * *\nL136: \nL137: ​\nL138: \nL139: [Input]\nL140: \nL141: [Button: Add to Cart]\nL142: \nL143: 【14†Request a Custom Order】\nL144: \nL145: Technical Service\nL146: \nL147: Need help? Our team of experienced scientists is here for you.\nL148: \nL149: 【15†Let Us Assist】\nL150: \nL151: * * *\nL152: \nL153: * * *\nL154: \nL155: Properties\nL156: \nL157: ### type\nL158: \nL159: Type I\nL160: \nL161: ### Quality Segment\nL162: \nL163: 【16†300】\nL164: \nL165: ### form\nL166: \nL167: fibers\nL168: ### color\nL169: \nL170: white\nL171: \nL172: ### storage temp.\nL173: \nL174: 2-8°C\nL175: \nL176: Description\nL177: \nL178: ### General description\nL179: \nL180: λmax_{ 259 nm} (100 mM phosphate buffer, pH 7.0).\nL181: DNA from calf thymus is 41.9 mole % G-C and 58.1 mole % A-T.1 An OD of 1.0 at 260 nm corresponds to ~ 50 μg of double-stranded DNA.\nL182: ### Application\nL183: \nL184: Calf thymus DNA (CT-DNA) is a natural DNA widely used in studies of DNA binding anticancer agents and DNA binding agents that modulate DNA structure and function. Calf thymus DNA is also used in physicochemical studies of DNA behavior in solution.\nL185: \nL186: ### Physical form\nL187: \nL188: fibrous preparation\nL189: ### Preparation Note\nL190: \nL191: Solutions of DNA have been stored successfully for several months at 4 C, pH 7.5-8, in 10 mM Tris with 1 mM EDTA and without a bacteriostatic agent. At low concentrations (μg/ml) DNA tends to absorb onto the surfaces of plastic tubes. It is not recommended to store DNA in highly alkaline solutions since DNA tends to degrade at alkaline pH greater than 8.0.\nL192: This product can be dissolved at 2 mg/ml in water. To reduce further shearing of the DNA, no sonication or stirring should be used. Gentle inversion overnight at 0-4 °C is recommended to completely solubilize the DNA. The presence of 1 mM EDTA is recommended to prevent nucleases from degrading the DNA.\nL193: \nL194: This product is extracted using a method that causes shearing yielding a highly polymerized mixture of double and single stranded DNA . However, double stranded DNA is the predominant form.\nL195: This product is prepared from calf thymus tissue of unspecified gender.\nL196: ### Analysis Note\nL197: \nL198: \"Highly Polymerized\"\nL199: \nL200: * * *\nL201: \nL202: ## Compare Similar Items\nL203: \nL204: 【17†View Full Comparison】\nL205: \nL206: * * *\nL207: \nL208: Show Differences\nL209: \nL210: [Input]\nL211: \nL212: 1 of 1\nL213: ###### This Item\nL214:  | D3664  | D4764  | D4522\nL215: --- | --- | --- | ---\nL216: 【18†Sigma-Aldrich D1501 Deoxyribonucleic acid sodium salt from calf thymus】[Button: Quick View]  | 【19†Sigma-Aldrich D3664 Deoxyribonucleic acid sodium salt from calf thymus】[Button: Quick View]  | 【20†Sigma-Aldrich D4764 Deoxyribonucleic acid from calf thymus】[Button: Quick View]  | 【21†Sigma-Aldrich D4522 Deoxyribonucleic acid from calf thymus】[Button: Quick 