u can still download Certificates of Analysis from our 【19†Documents】 section.\nL226: \nL227: If you need assistance, please contact 【11†Customer Support】\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n (https://www.ccap.ac.uk/wp-content/uploads/MR_Walnes.pdf)\nciteturn12view3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: application/pdf; Number of pages: 1; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.ccap.ac.uk/wp-content/uploads/MR_Walnes.pdf\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 40\nL0@P0: WALNE'S MEDIUM FOR ALGAL CULTURES\nL1@P0: Recommended for large volumes of aquaculture strains\nL2@P0: Stocks  per 100 ml\nL3@P0: (1)  Trace metal solution (TMS)\nL4@P0: ZnCl2  2.1 g\nL5@P0: CoCl2.6H2O  2.0 g\nL6@P0: (NH4)6Mo7O24.4H2O  0.9 g\nL7@P0: CuSO4.5H2O  2.0 g\nL8@P0: Make  up  to 100  ml with distilled  water.  This solution is  normally\nL9@P0: cloudy.  Acidify with a few drops of conc. HCl to give a clear solution.\nL10@P0: (2)  Vitamin solution\nL11@P0: Vitamin B12. (Cyanocobalamin)  10.0 mg\nL12@P0: Vitamin B1  (Thiamine.HCl)  10.0 mg\nL13@P0: Vitamin H   (Biotin)  200.0 µg\nL14@P0: Make up to 100 ml with distilled water.\nL15@P0: per litre\nL16@P0: (3)  Nutrient solution\nL17@P0: FeCl3.6H20  1.3 g\nL18@P0: MnCl2.4H20  0.36 g\nL19@P0: H3BO3  33.6 g\nL20@P0: EDTA(Disodium salt)  45.0 g\nL21@P0: NaH2PO4.2H2O  20.0 g\nL22@P0: NaNO3  100.0 g\nL23@P0: TMS (1 above)  1.0 ml\nL24@P0: Make up to 1 litre with distilled water.\nL25@P0: Medium per litre\nL26@P0: Nutrient solution (3)  1.0 ml\nL27@P0: Vitamin solution (2)  0.1 ml\nL28@P0: Sterilised seawater  1.0 litre\nL29@P0: Dispense nutrient and vitamin solutions separately into 10 ml and 1 ml respectively\nL30@P0: and autoclave at 15 psi for 15 minutes.  Add an aliquot of each aseptically to 10\nL31@P0: litres of sterilised seawater.\nL32@P0: Reference\nL33@P0: Walne PR (1970) Studies on the food value of nineteen genera of algae to juvenile\nL34@P0: bivalves  of the  genera Ostrea, Crassostrea, Mercenaria,  and Mytilis.  Fish.  Invest. 26, 1­62.\nL35@P0: 7 August 2002\nL36@P0: media r\nL37@P0: ecipes\nL38@P0: CCAP (Culture Collection of Algae and Protozoa), Dunstaffnage Marine Laboratory,  Oban, Argyll, PA37 1QA, UK\nL39@P0: Tel: +44 (0)1631 559000  Fax: +44 (0)1631 559001  Email: ccap@sams.ac.uk Web: www.ccap.ac.uk\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n1060 (https://www.dsmz.de/microorganisms/medium/pdf/DSMZ_Medium590.pdf)\nciteturn12view4 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 3 days ago; Content type: application/pdf; Number of pages: 1; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.dsmz.de/microorganisms/medium/pdf/DSMZ_Medium590.pdf\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 41\nL0@P0: © 2007 DSMZ GmbH - All rights reserved\nL1@P0: 590. DICHOTOMICROBIUM THERMOHALOPHILUM MEDIUM\nL2@P0: Bacto Yeast extract (Difco) 1.000 g\nL3@P0: Na2-DL-malate 1.000 g\nL4@P0: Hutner's basal salts 20.000 ml\nL5@P0: Artifical sea water, 3 times conc. 980.000 ml\nL6@P0: pH 7.0-7.2\nL7@P0: Agar at a concentration of 18 g/l is added for solid media.\nL8@P0: Prepare an 8% solution of NaHCO3 in half full 100ml serum bottles closed with a rubber\nL9@P0: septum and autoclave. Add 28.4 ml of the sterile 8% solution of NaHCO3 (2.822g/l) per\nL10@P0: litre of the sterile, cooled medium.\nL11@P0: Artificial sea water, 3 times concentrated:\nL12@P0: NaCl 70.430 g\nL13@P0: Na2SO4 11.750 g\nL14@P0: KCl 1.990 g\nL15@P0: KBr 0.290 g\nL16@P0: MgCl2 x 6 H2O 31.860 g\nL17@P0: CaCl2 x 2 H2O 4.350 g\nL18@P0: H3BO3 0.080 g\nL19@P0: Distilled water 1000.000 ml\nL20@P0: Hutner's salts:\nL21@P0: Nitrilotriacetic acid (NTA) 10.000 g\nL22@P0: MgSO4 x 7 H2O 29.700 g\nL23@P0: CaCl2 x 2 H2O 3.335 g\nL24@P0: (NH4)6MoO7O24 x 4 H2O 9.250 mg\nL25@P0: FeSO4 x 7 H2O 99.000 mg\nL26@P0: \"Metals 44\" 50.000 ml\nL27@P0: Distilled water 950.000 ml\nL28@P0: Dissolve the nitrilotriacetic acid, adjust the pH to 7.0 with KOH (about 7.3 g). Dissolve\nL29@P0: other salts separately, combine and adjust the pH to 6.8 with NaOH or H2SO4.\nL30@P0: \"Metals 44\":\nL31@P0: Na-EDTA 250.000 mg\nL32@P0: ZnSO4 x 7 H2O 1095.000 mg\nL33@P0: FeSO4 x 7 H2O 500.000 mg\nL34@P0: MnSO4 x H2O 154.000 mg\nL35@P0: CuSO4 x 5 H2O 39.200 mg\nL36@P0: Co(NO3)2 x 6 H2O 24.800 mg\nL37@P0: Na2B4O7 x 10 H2O 17.700 mg\nL38@P0: Distilled water 1000.000 ml\nL39@P0: Dissolve the EDTA and add a few drops of concentrated H2SO4 to retard precipitation of\nL40@P0: the heavy metal ions.\n"
